{"s1_door_welcome_sign_051","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=funny|world=door",{1,"We should probably take down the sign on the gate",2,"Which one, beware of dog?",1,"No, the painted one your mother made, y'all come on in, the door's always open"}},
{"s1_door_same_one_back_052","any",3,"reg=civilian|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=grim",{1,"That's the same one from yesterday, the mailman with the one shoe",2,"How can you tell?",3,"The satchel, he's still carrying his satchel",1,"Still on his route, every morning about nine"}},
{"s1_kids_six_times_001","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,10|mood=sad",{1,"Emily asked about her daddy again, that's six times since breakfast",2,"What'd you tell her this time?",1,"That he's working a double at the plant, same as the other five",2,"She'll quit believing it one of these days",1,"I know, I'm just counting on her staying four a little bit longer"}},
{"s1_kids_bike_roads_002","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,12|mood=angry|world=road",{1,"Dad's truck could be anywhere between here and the base - I could take the ten-speed and check the back roads",2,"No",1,"You didn't even let me finish!",2,"I let you finish yesterday - and Tuesday, it's still no"}},
{"s1_kids_pager_code_003","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,3|hour=4,11|mood=fear",{1,"His pager went off in the junk drawer this morning - he forgot it here Friday",2,"Who's paging him?",1,"It was our code, four-one-one, call home, the one we made up, I didn't send it",2,"Then he's alive, he's somewhere with a phone",1,"Or somebody's pushing buttons on his, I don't know which one to pray on"}},
{"s1_kids_crayon_box_004","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=sad",{1,"She drew the family for me, me, her, the dog, the house with smoke out the chimney",2,"Where's Mike in it?",1,"Little box way off in the corner, I asked what the box was",1,"She said it's his truck, he's still driving home"}},
{"s1_kids_dorm_phone_005","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,4|mood=fear",{1,"Kevin's dorm phone was busy all Friday night. Busy, not ringing. Somebody had to be using it",2,"Or it's off the hook",3,"Why would you say that to her?",2,"I'm scared too, okay? I shouldn't have said it like that. It's probably just busy"}},
{"s1_kids_his_chair_006","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=sad|world=window",{1,"Jacob won't let anybody sit in his daddy's chair, pitched a fit when I moved it to reach the window",2,"Let him have the chair",1,"I did, I put it back - I put the crossword back on the arm too"}},
{"s1_kids_walkman_batteries_007","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=angry",{1,"Can I have two double-As? Just two, for my Walkman",2,"Those are flashlight batteries now",1,"I've been listening to the same tape in my head for three days - it's making me crazy",2,"Two, and you're taking the late watch for them"}},
{"s1_kids_irvington_girl_008","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=sad|world=building",{1,"Stacy lives out past Irvington, we were supposed to go to the fair together",2,"Her daddy's a hunter, they've got guns in that house, and a cellar",1,"I still have her class ring, she made me wear it on my pinky 'cause it was too small"}},
{"s1_kids_monster_question_009","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=grim",{1,"Sarah asked me straight out if her daddy's one of the monsters now",2,"Lord, what did you say?",1,"I said I didn't know, she said okay and went back to her coloring",1,"She took it better than I did, hon, that's what scares me"}},
{"s1_kids_library_game_010","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=warm",{1,"We're playing the library game again, quietest one by supper gets the last pack of peanut butter crackers",2,"How long's that going to hold 'em?",1,"Longer than it holds me, I've been dying to talk since lunch"}},
{"s1_kids_eggless_cake_011","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=4,8|mood=warm",{1,"Maddie's birthday is the seventeenth, she's turning seven",2,"We've got a box of cake mix, no eggs, no oil",1,"Mamaw used to do mayonnaise instead of eggs, swore by it",2,"Then we're making a mayonnaise cake - don't tell her what's in it"}},
{"s1_kids_saw_crying_012","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|hour=20,3|mood=sad|world=door,building",{1,"I saw you in the pantry, with the door shut",2,"I was counting the cans",1,"In the dark?",2,"Go to bed, sweetheart - mama's fine"}},
{"s1_kids_nursing_home_013","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,6|mood=fear",{1,"Somebody needs to call the nursing home in Brandenburg about Grandma",2,"I called, it's a recording, due to the current situation, visiting hours are suspended",3,"Visiting hours, like we're just dropping by with a potted plant",1,"She hates potted plants, she'd tell you so to your face"}},
{"s1_kids_mutter_husband_014","any",1,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|hour=21,4|mood=sad",{1,"Kids are asleep, Jim, both of them - Katie finally quit asking",1,"I put your flannel on her pillow - it helps - don't ask me why",1,"Come home soon, okay? I'm running out of things to say to her"}},
{"s1_kids_note_on_door_015","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=grim|world=door,road",{1,"If we leave, he comes home to an empty house",2,"We tape a note inside the storm door, where we went, what day, what road",1,"And if one of them tears the note down?",2,"Then we paint it on the garage door in letters a foot high - settled?",1,"Settled"}},
{"s1_kids_summer_school_016","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=funny",{1,"Look on the bright side, no summer school for algebra",2,"You'd rather have monsters than Mr. Hubbard?",1,"Mr. Hubbard gave me a D. The monsters haven't graded me yet",3,"Don't jinx it"}},
{"s1_kids_deputy_dad_017","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,8|mood=fear|world=vehicle,road",{1,"My dad's a deputy, he'll be out on the roads helping people, that's why he's late",2,"Yeah, yeah, that makes sense",1,"You believe me, right?",2,"He gave me a ride home from the pool once - in the back of the cruiser, he's the kind who'd be helping"}},
{"s1_kids_goldfish_018","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=warm",{1,"Bubbles died - the goldfish, tank filter quit",2,"Does Tyler know?",1,"He wants a funeral, in the flower bed, with a prayer",2,"Then we give that fish the best funeral in Knox County"}},
{"s1_kids_tell_her_019","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=angry|world=building",{1,"If Lily asks me where Dad is one more time I'm just gonna tell her",2,"Tell her what? You don't know anything",1,"I know he's not coming, everybody in this house knows it but her",2,"You don't know that, and you'll keep your mouth shut, because she's six"}},
{"s1_kids_twentytwo_020","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=calm|world=fence",{1,"Breathe out slow, squeeze, don't pull, your grandpa taught me on this same rifle",2,"What were you shooting at?",1,"Pop cans on a fence post out in Ekron",2,"Did you hit any?",1,"We're not talking about me - squeeze"}},
{"s1_kids_supposed_to_021","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=sad|world=building",{1,"When the tornado siren went off last spring, I had everybody in the basement in two minutes flat",2,"I remember",1,"I'm supposed to be the one that knows what to do when the siren goes - there's no siren for this"}},
{"s1_kids_rubbed_back_022","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=warm|world=stairs",{1,"I sat down on the stairs and just lost it - couldn't help it",2,"Did the boys see?",1,"Little one came and sat one step up and rubbed my shoulder - said, deep breaths, like at the dentist",1,"That's what I tell him at the dentist"}},
{"s1_kids_go_fish_023","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=4,14|mood=funny",{1,"Go Fish again?",2,"We've played Go Fish forty times - I've counted",3,"The deck's missing the three of hearts anyway",1,"So we play Go Fish and nobody asks for threes - see? Problem solved"}},
{"s1_kids_rosewood_friends_024","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=sad",{1,"The whole team lives in Rosewood - Brandon, Luis, the Keller twins",2,"Rosewood's got a fire station, and the school gym, people would go there",1,"We had a game on the tenth, against March Ridge",2,"I know, bud"}},
{"s1_kids_formula_025","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|hour=4,9|mood=fear",{1,"We've got four days of formula, five if I water it down",2,"Don't water it down",1,"Then four",2,"The pharmacy on Main has a baby aisle, I'll go at first light"}},
{"s1_kids_monster_game_026","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=fear|world=building",{1,"The boys were playing monsters in the hallway, arms out, moaning, chasing each other",2,"Oh, no",1,"I yelled harder than I ever had. They hid in their room. I still hate remembering it",2,"You were frightened. I hope you got to tell them that instead of leaving them guessing"}},
{"s1_kids_camcorder_027","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|hour=19,23|mood=sad",{1,"She wants to watch the Fourth of July tape again",2,"That's the eighth time today, the VCR's gonna eat it",3,"Let her watch, it's the only part where he talks - he's the one holding the camera",2,"Fine - Rewind it slow, then"}},
{"s1_kids_mower_028","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=funny",{1,"When Dad gets back I'm gonna tell him I wrecked the riding mower into the shed",2,"You wrecked the mower?",1,"In June, hid it with a tarp - I figure now's the time, he'll be too happy to yell"}},
{"s1_kids_jacket_029","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=4,14|hour=16,5|mood=angry|world=cold",{1,"That's Dad's jacket - take it off",2,"It's cold at night and he isn't using it",1,"Take - it - off",3,"Both of you knock it off, you each get it every other night - starting with nobody tonight"}},
{"s1_kids_valley_station_030","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=grim|world=vehicle,building",{1,"Listen close, if I get bit, you take your sister to Aunt Linda's in Valley Station",2,"I don't know the way",1,"Dixie Highway north, left at the car wash, blue house with the ugly geese on the porch",2,"Say it again - slower"}},
{"s1_kids_mixtape_031","any",1,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=sad",{1,"Dad made this tape for our trip to Gatlinburg, he talks between the songs like a radio man",1,"Side B he says, next one's for the lady in the passenger seat, and Mom always hit him",1,"I only play side B when the batteries are fresh - so it doesn't go slow"}},
{"s1_kids_bedwet_032","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=warm",{1,"Noah wet the bed again, first time since he was four - he's so embarrassed",2,"Tell him I spilled a whole glass of water on mine",1,"You did?",2,"I will in about five minutes"}},
{"s1_kids_sneaking_out_033","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|hour=0,5|mood=angry",{1,"Where were you? Your bed's been empty an hour",2,"Just over at the Dawsons' - Jess is scared by herself",1,"Her whole family's in that house",2,"Her whole family's not the same as me, Mom"}},
{"s1_kids_army_today_034","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|hour=6,10|mood=sad|world=window",{1,"First thing out of her mouth every morning: Is the Army coming today?",2,"What do you tell her?",1,"Maybe today, and she goes and sits by the front window with her juice"}},
{"s1_kids_toilet_035","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=5,14|mood=funny",{1,"Why can't we flush anymore?",2,"We're saving water, sweetie - remember?",1,"Grandpa's saving a lot of water in there",3,"Well, she ain't wrong, Daddy"}},
{"s1_kids_letter_taped_036","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=sad|world=door",{1,"She wrote her daddy a letter and taped it to the front door - facing out",2,"What's it say?",1,"Dear Daddy, the key is under the frog - love, Hannah, and then about fifteen X's"}},
{"s1_kids_echo_creek_farm_037","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14",{1,"Papaw and Mamaw's place out at Echo Creek has the well and the chickens - we ought to be there",2,"Nobody's heard from them since Thursday",3,"Mamaw never picks up anyhow, she thinks the phone's for emergencies",1,"Well, it's an emergency"}},
{"s1_kids_scout_camp_038","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,6|mood=fear",{1,"Danny's at Scout camp till Sunday, there's forty boys out there and three dads",2,"Scoutmaster Lewis is a good man, he was a Marine",1,"He sells insurance!",2,"He was a Marine before that, he'll keep 'em together, I know he will"}},
{"s1_kids_scared_ashamed_039","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=warm|world=stairs,building",{1,"I froze on the stairs when it came in the kitchen - you had to do everything",2,"You're seventeen",1,"That's supposed to be old enough",2,"I'm forty-one and my knees were knocking so loud I thought it'd hear 'em - we're square"}},
{"s1_kids_laser_photo_040","any",1,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=sad",{1,"Best picture of Ray I've got is his work badge - from the plant",1,"Worst haircut of his life, he hid that badge from me for a year",1,"Now it's in the frame by the bed, he'd be so mad"}},
{"s1_kids_shell_casings_041","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=grim",{1,"Luke's got a jar of shell casings from the yard - he counts them before bed",2,"Take the jar away",1,"I tried, he said every one of them is a monster that didn't get us - so I gave it back"}},
{"s1_kids_muldraugh_dad_042","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|mood=sad",{1,"It was his weekend, I was supposed to drop them off at his apartment in Muldraugh on Friday",2,"And you didn't",1,"I was running late, I was always running late on his weekends - he used to get so mad about it"}},
{"s1_kids_stepdad_043","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=warm",{1,"I never called you Dad, not once in three years",2,"I noticed",1,"You still went back out for me, to the pool house",2,"Well, you still don't have to call me anything, pass the peaches"}},
{"s1_kids_quiet_bedtime_044","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=1,14|hour=20,23|mood=warm",{1,"Story time, but whisper voices only",2,"Can it be the one about the bear who ate the pancakes?",3,"That one's got a roaring part",1,"The bear's got a sore throat tonight, he roars real quiet"}},
{"s1_kids_count_heads_045","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=0,14|mood=fear|world=building",{1,"One, two, three - where's four?",2,"She's in the bathroom!",1,"You tell me when anybody leaves this room - anybody, even the bathroom",2,"I'm sorry, Mama, I'll tell you, I promise"}},
{"s1_kids_weekday_confusion_046","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=5,14|mood=calm",{1,"Is it Sunday? Should we have church?",2,"It's {weekday}, baby",1,"Can we have church anyway?",2,"Sure, go get the Bible and pick us a short one"}},
{"s1_kids_school_clothes_047","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=6,14|mood=sad|world=building",{1,"We bought her school clothes last weekend, sale at the mall in Louisville",2,"The purple overalls?",1,"Tags are still on, she tried them on in the living room and wouldn't take them off till bath"}},
{"s1_kids_telling_older_048","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=4,14|hour=21,2|mood=grim|world=vehicle",{1,"You're old enough, so I'm telling you and not your brother - your uncle's not in the hospital",2,"I know",1,"How long have you known?",2,"I saw the car in the side yard, I just didn't want you to have to say it"}},
{"s1_kids_braces_049","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=funny",{1,"I was supposed to get my braces off on the fifteenth",2,"Sorry, kiddo - Dr. Hale's office is closed till further notice",1,"So I'm gonna survive the end of the world with a mouth full of rubber bands",2,"Straightest teeth in the county, though"}},
{"s1_kids_grown_up_word_050","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=2,14|mood=funny",{1,"Who taught Jesse that word? He said it at the thing in the yard",2,"Wasn't me",3,"It was a little bit you",2,"He used it right, though, you got to give him that"}},
{"s1_kids_two_kinds_bread_051","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=3,14|mood=sad",{1,"I cut the crusts off Abby's sandwich like her dad does - she wouldn't eat it",2,"Why not?",1,"I cut them wrong, he does triangles - I did squares"}},
{"s1_kids_tired_teen_052","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=fresh|day=5,14|hour=16,5|mood=calm",{1,"You can sleep in your own room tonight, you don't have to sleep on our floor anymore",2,"Can I sleep on the floor anyway?",1,"Grab your pillow"}},
{"s2_c01_seed_catalog_001","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=195,245|hour=18,23|mood=warm|world=building",{1,"Found a seed catalog in the Dunns' mailbox, came the week after the Fourth and nobody ever opened it",2,"Read the tomato page again",1,"Beefsteak - Meaty, deep red, fruits up to two pounds - Resists cracking",3,"Resists cracking, wish I did",2,"Hush - keep going, do the cantaloupe"}},
{"s2_c01_good_friday_potatoes_002","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=256,272|hour=20,5|mood=calm|world=snow",{1,"Papaw put his potatoes in the ground on Good Friday - every year, rain or shine",2,"Do we even know when Good Friday is?",1,"I counted from the last frost and the moon, and I say it's tomorrow",2,"You counted from the moon",1,"Cut the seed potatoes tonight, two eyes a piece - let 'em scab over skin-side down"}},
{"s2_c01_scarecrow_suit_003","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=265,390|hour=16,22|mood=funny|world=building",{1,"Who dressed the scarecrow in a church suit?",2,"Only clothes in the Methodist closet that weren't choir robes",3,"I about put a round through it at dusk, standing out there in a necktie like a deacon",2,"Then it works, it was never for the crows - crows don't care about anything"}},
{"s2_c01_hair_in_hose_004","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=250,380|mood=funny|world=fence",{1,"Deer got the bean rows down to stubs again",2,"Mamaw hung human hair in old pantyhose along the fence - deer smell people and stay off",1,"We did haircuts Sunday, there's a whole grocery sack of hair",2,"Well then, first time your hair's ever been useful to anybody"}},
{"s2_c01_maple_sap_005","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=205,240|hour=7,17|mood=calm|world=door",{1,"Sap's running, buckets on the sugar maples behind the church are near full",2,"Forty gallons of that to make one of syrup - forty",3,"And a fire going all day, putting up smoke anybody on the ridge can see",1,"Then we boil it in the barn with the big doors open - smoke goes out low and flat",3,"You've thought about this",1,"Since October"}},
{"s2_c01_dry_land_fish_006","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=272,300|mood=warm|world=water",{1,"Dry-land fish are up, under the dead elms by the creek, just like Daddy said",2,"You sure those are the good ones? Not the fake kind that'll put you in the ground?",1,"Cut one longways - Hollow all the way through, top to bottom, that's the good ones",2,"Then I'm getting out the lard, I been saving that lard since Christmas for exactly this"}},
{"s2_c01_poke_three_waters_007","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=275,315|mood=calm|world=fence",{1,"Poke's coming up along the fence, young leaves, before the stalks go purple",2,"Boil it in three waters, pour off every one, my granny near died of the second water once",1,"Why'd she drink the second water?",2,"She never drank it, she skipped it, you're telling it wrong"}},
{"s2_c01_jar_pings_008","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=45,130|hour=20,23|mood=calm|world=building",{1,"Seven jars on the counter, that's six pings",2,"Give it an hour, some lids are slow",1,"It's been two hours, I'm lying awake listening to a jar",2,"Put the quiet one at the front of the cellar shelf - we eat that one first"}},
{"s2_c01_potato_eyes_009","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=240,275|mood=grim|world=building",{1,"Root cellar potatoes are sprouting, eyes long as my finger",2,"Snap 'em off and eat the firm ones first, the soft ones are seed",1,"Half the bin's soft",2,"Then half the bin's next year, and we eat a lot of beans between now and June"}},
{"s2_c01_hog_killing_010","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=125,175|mood=grim",{1,"It's hog-killing weather, first real freeze, and that sow in the Crider pen is eating acorns we could be eating",2,"Anybody here actually done it? Not watched - done it",3,"I held the pan at my uncle's once, I was nine and I cried",1,"Then you're foreman, I got the extension office pamphlet with the drawings",2,"A crier and a pamphlet, that hog's got better odds than we do"}},
{"s2_c01_broody_hen_011","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=250,340|hour=16,5|mood=funny|world=door",{1,"Dot's gone broody, she's been sitting on two golf balls and a doorknob since Tuesday",2,"Put real eggs under her",1,"I tried, she pecked me bloody and rolled the doorknob back under",2,"Give her real ones tonight and leave the doorknob, it's hers now"}},
{"s2_c01_chicks_hatched_012","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=285,345|mood=warm",{1,"Come look in the box, quiet",2,"Lord, how many?",1,"Six out of eight, the last one pecked its way out an hour ago",3,"That's the first thing born on this place since everything",2,"Nobody name them, you name them and then you can't eat them",3,"Too late - Carla already named the little yellow one Supper"}},
{"s2_c01_goat_seed_packets_013","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=200,300|mood=angry",{1,"That goat ate the seed packets, every carrot and half the lettuce",2,"I told you she eats paper, she ate Earl's hat off his head",1,"Carrot seed, Rhonda! There's no feed store to go get more carrot seed!",2,"Then we watch where she goes for a couple days and see what comes up"}},
{"s2_c01_milking_lesson_014","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=200,400|hour=5,8|mood=funny",{1,"Squeeze from the top down, thumb and first finger close it off, then roll the rest",2,"I'm rolling - nothing's coming",3,"She's looking back at you like you owe her money",1,"She can tell you're scared - hum something",2,"I am not humming to a goat",3,"He's humming"}},
{"s2_c01_trotline_turtle_015","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,130|hour=5,10|mood=calm",{1,"Ran the trotline at daylight, four hooks cleaned, two channel cats, and a turtle mad as a hornet",2,"What'd you do with the turtle?",1,"Brought it",2,"I'm not cleaning a snapping turtle before breakfast",1,"Then after, it's not going anywhere in that bucket but mad"}},
{"s2_c01_breaking_ice_016","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=178,230|hour=6,9|mood=grim|world=building",{1,"Ice on the barrel's two inches this morning, took the hatchet to it",2,"Bring the chunks in, melt 'em on the stove",1,"Stove's got the beans on",2,"Then set 'em next to the beans, everything in this house shares"}},
{"s2_c01_snow_to_water_017","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=180,235|mood=calm|world=snow",{1,"Ten buckets of snow, and I got a bucket and a half of water",2,"And there's grass in it",1,"It's snow off the yard, there's gonna be some yard in it",2,"Strain it through a T-shirt, the clean one, not that one"}},
{"s2_c01_acorn_coffee_018","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=95,220|mood=funny|world=rain,hot",{1,"Acorn coffee, shelled, soaked a week to leach the bitter out, roasted in the skillet",2,"It's brown and it's hot",3,"That's two of the three things coffee's supposed to be",1,"What's the third?",3,"Coffee"}},
{"s2_c01_mutter_cupholder_beans_019","any",1,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=40,400",{1,"Three coffee beans in a cup holder - real ones, rolling around with a penny and a bobby pin",1,"Chewed one right there - put the other two in my shirt pocket",1,"Gonna be smelling that pocket till Christmas"}},
{"s2_c01_solar_shower_020","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=330,400|hour=13,18|mood=funny",{1,"Black trash bag's been hanging in the sun since breakfast - water's warm",2,"I'm first",3,"You were first yesterday",2,"I was first yesterday because I'm the one that filled it yesterday",1,"I filled it today, so I'm first, and you two can stand out here and argue in the smell"}},
{"s2_c01_funeral_fans_021","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,80|hour=12,18|mood=funny",{1,"Took a box of paper fans out of the Baptist church - the kind on a popsicle stick",2,"Every one's got the funeral home printed on the back - serving families since 1948",1,"They'd have had a real good summer",2,"Don't - just fan"}},
{"s2_c01_sawdust_ice_022","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=340,400|hour=11,19|mood=warm|world=building,water",{1,"Come down the cellar a minute, bring a glass",2,"What for?",1,"Put up creek ice in sawdust back in January, y'all laughed at me, there's one chunk left",3,"In July?",1,"In July, it's about the size of a biscuit - get the glasses, all of you"}},
{"s2_c01_ice_storm_limbs_023","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=208,222|hour=21,4|mood=fear|world=trees",{1,"That's another limb, sounds just like a rifle",2,"Ice storm, every tree in the county's coming apart tonight",1,"How do you know it's limbs?",2,"Because there's been forty of 'em since dark, and nobody's got that much ammo"}},
{"s2_c01_snow_tracks_024","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=182,235|hour=6,10|mood=fear|world=window,snow",{1,"Fresh snow - look at the yard",2,"Tracks, all the way around the house - twice",3,"Shuffling ones, drags a foot, it stopped a good while under the kids' window",1,"Then that window gets the dresser tonight, and nobody tells the kids why"}},
{"s2_c01_snow_cream_025","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=182,235|hour=16,5|mood=warm|world=snow",{1,"Snow cream! Mama made it every winter, snow, sugar, a can of milk, a little vanilla",2,"Not off the first snow, first snow's dirty, it cleans the air on the way down",3,"When's the second snow?",2,"Tonight, maybe, if you go to sleep real fast",3,"I'm asleep, I'm already asleep"}},
{"s2_c01_dandelion_greens_026","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=255,290|mood=funny",{1,"Dandelion greens - Wilted down in bacon grease",2,"Tastes like mowing the yard",1,"I used to pay a boy five dollars to mow that yard",2,"And now I'm eating it for free, moving up in the world"}},
{"s2_c01_sassafras_027","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=245,300|mood=calm|world=fence",{1,"Dug sassafras root out of the fence row, spring tonic, Mamaw called it",2,"Tonic for what?",1,"She never said, you drank it in March and you didn't ask",2,"Smells like root beer, that woman ran the same con on this family for forty years"}},
{"s2_c01_rifle_season_028","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=118,135|mood=grim|world=vehicle,road",{1,"Opening day of rifle season, not one pickup pulled off along the Rosewood road",2,"Used to be you couldn't find a place to park",1,"Deer are standing in the middle of the road like they heard the news",2,"They heard, they're not the ones getting hunted this year"}},
{"s2_c01_frog_gigging_029","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=320,400|hour=21,1|mood=funny|world=water",{1,"Frog gigging tonight, flashlight, gig, burlap sack",2,"A flashlight on the pond at night, might as well ring the church bell",3,"Tape red cellophane over the lens, coon hunters did it so the whole holler didn't see 'em",2,"The frogs don't care what color it is, I'm not worried about the frogs",1,"I'm going, legs rolled in cornmeal - anybody wants some carries the sack"}},
{"s2_c01_chiggers_polish_030","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,90|mood=funny|world=building",{1,"Chiggers got me from the berry patch clear up to my belt line",2,"Clear nail polish on every bite - Smothers 'em",1,"Only polish in this house is Mandy's, the bottle says Flamingo Kiss",2,"Then you're a big pink polka-dot man for about a week - hold still"}},
{"s2_c01_cellar_popcorn_031","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=60,400|hour=18,22|mood=funny|world=stairs,building",{1,"Found a jar of popcorn kernels behind the flour, old, but they rattle right",2,"Popcorn pops - Popping is a noise",3,"Do it in the cellar with the lid on, and everybody sits on the stairs",1,"Every pop, I swear I'm gonna flinch",2,"Flinch and chew, we've gotten real good at that"}},
{"s2_c01_outgrown_boots_032","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=100,400|mood=calm",{1,"Toby used to outgrow boots before we'd paid for them",2,"Feet don't know about any of this, they just keep on growing",1,"I remember looking for kid sizes on the top shelf of a shoe store",2,"I'd buy two sizes up now, if I ever had the choice. Never appreciated having a choice"}},
{"s2_c01_garden_labels_033","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=250,330|mood=sad|world=fence",{1,"Found Glenn's garden labels in the coffee can, popsicle sticks, in his writing",2,"What's on them?",1,"Silver Queen - Kentucky Wonder, rattlesnake beans, with a little snake drawn on it",2,"Plant it the way he had it, then",1,"Beans go by the fence, he always put the beans by the fence"}},
{"s2_c01_second_summer_034","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=335,400|hour=12,17|mood=grim|world=building",{1,"Second summer, I was hoping the first one was a fluke",2,"Kentucky don't do flukes, it does July",1,"Last year I had a whole list of things I missed - now I just miss being dry",2,"Go sit in the root cellar a spell, it's sixty down there",1,"I'm moving down there, pass my supper through the hatch"}},
{"s2_c01_screen_porch_035","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh,seasoned|day=15,70|hour=21,2|mood=calm|world=door,building",{1,"Anybody sleeping on the screened porch tonight?",2,"Screen's got holes, mosquitoes use 'em like doors",3,"And one of them things could walk right up to that screen and watch you sleep",1,"I'll take watched, it's ninety in that bedroom",2,"Take the shotgun and a bedsheet, then, wet the sheet first"}},
{"s2_c01_trash_can_filter_036","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,200|mood=calm|world=building",{1,"Trash can filter's done, gravel on the bottom, then sand, then charcoal out of the stove",2,"It's still brown coming out",1,"It's clearer brown, you boil it after",2,"Clearer brown - write that on the can so nobody drinks straight out of it"}},
{"s2_c01_blackberry_wine_037","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=45,200|mood=funny",{1,"Blackberry wine's been working in the crock three weeks - it's fizzing",2,"Is it supposed to fizz?",1,"The recipe don't say it's not",3,"Where'd you get a wine recipe?",1,"Back of the church cookbook, grandma Tuttle wrote it in pencil under her jam, real small",3,"In the Baptist cookbook, grandma Tuttle was a sly old thing"}},
{"s2_c01_sunday_tape_038","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=40,250|hour=18,22|mood=warm|world=stairs,generator",{1,"Sunday, generator gets one hour, vote on the tape",2,"The Christmas tape - nineteen ninety, uncle Dave falls off the ladder",3,"We've watched him fall off that ladder nine Sundays running",2,"And he falls off so good every single time",1,"Christmas tape wins, somebody go get the extension cord"}},
{"s2_c01_thanksgiving_table_039","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=134,142|mood=warm",{1,"Thanksgiving, near as I can figure - fourth Thursday",2,"No turkey",3,"There was a turkey, in the Pruitts' bottom field - I missed it",1,"We got two squirrels, a pan of cornbread, and sweet potatoes out of our own dirt",2,"Go around the table, then, one thing each - keep it short",3,"The woodstove"}},
{"s2_c01_cedar_tree_040","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=158,170|mood=warm|world=fence",{1,"Cut a cedar out of the fence row - it's crooked",2,"Every cedar in Kentucky's crooked - stand it in the bucket",3,"What do we hang on it?",1,"Can lids, punch a hole, run a string through - they'll catch the lamplight",3,"Can I do the top one?",1,"You can do the top one"}},
{"s2_c01_santa_fence_041","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=150,168|mood=warm|world=fence,road",{1,"Missy asked me can Santa get through the Army fence",2,"Lord, and you said?",1,"Said Santa don't need a road, said he goes right over the top",2,"Then Santa and me are going to the Rosewood drugstore Thursday - early"}},
{"s2_c01_new_year_042","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=175,177|hour=22,2|mood=funny",{1,"Is it midnight?",2,"My watch says eleven-fifty, his says one",3,"Split the difference, happy New Year",1,"My resolution's to quit smoking",2,"You haven't had a cigarette since August",1,"And I'm real proud of myself for sticking with it"}},
{"s2_c01_groundhog_043","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=206,210|mood=funny",{1,"Groundhog Day, saw one come out from under the barn",2,"Did it see its shadow?",1,"Never got the chance, it's in the pot",2,"So that's six more weeks of stew"}},
{"s2_c01_derby_goats_044","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=299,305|hour=16,19|mood=warm|world=building",{1,"First Saturday in May - Derby's today, if anybody was running it",2,"Daddy'd have the radio out on the porch and a bourbon he called his medicine",3,"Race the goats, then - Loser does dishes",1,"Goats won't run in a straight line",3,"Neither did any horse Daddy ever bet on"}},
{"s2_c01_flag_fourth_045","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=356,361|mood=calm|world=building,road",{1,"Pop wants to fly the flag tomorrow, off the porch rail",2,"Flag can be seen from the road",1,"Anybody close enough to see that flag can already see the house",2,"Fly it, then, it's the only thing on this place that's been through worse"}},
{"s2_c01_one_year_046","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=364,367|mood=grim",{1,"A year today - the ninth",2,"It's a Saturday this time",1,"Still the ninth",2,"Still the ninth - you want to do something for it?",1,"No, I want to do the chores same as yesterday and wake up and have it be the tenth"}},
{"s2_c02_picket_crosses_001","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,120|mood=grim|world=fence",{1,"Pulled pickets off the Hensleys' fence for the crosses, they were white once",2,"Write the names in paint pen this time, not marker - marker ran off Leon's in a week",1,"I know it did, I've written Leon three times now",2,"Paint pen's in the glovebox, do Leon's first"}},
{"s2_c02_daffodil_bulbs_002","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=100,135|mood=sad",{1,"Dug daffodil bulbs out of the flower bed at the old house - planting them on the graves",2,"Ground's getting hard",1,"Six inches down, pointy end up, they'll come up in March like nothing ever happened",2,"Give me the trowel, I'll do Mama's"}},
{"s2_c02_daffodils_up_003","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=245,275|mood=warm",{1,"Come out to the graves - before breakfast",2,"What's wrong?",1,"Nothing's wrong, the daffodils came up",3,"Every one of them?",1,"Every one but Uncle Pete's, his came up a day late - figures"}},
{"s2_c02_reel_mower_graves_004","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=270,400|mood=calm|world=building",{1,"Mowed around the graves with the old reel mower - quiet as a pair of scissors",2,"You do the edges?",1,"On my knees with the kitchen shears, didn't seem right leaving 'em shaggy",2,"Mama'd have made you do it twice"}},
{"s2_c02_frozen_ground_005","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=185,230|mood=grim|world=door",{1,"Ground's froze a foot down - pick bounces right off it",2,"Then Mr. Haskell stays in the shed till it thaws",3,"In the shed, with the lawnmower",2,"Wrapped in the good tarp, door wired shut, we made sure of him first - he'll keep"}},
{"s2_c02_stranger_cross_006","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,300|mood=sad",{1,"What do I paint on the stranger's cross?",2,"Man in a blue jacket... that's all we got",1,"Somebody out there knows his name and is looking for him right now",2,"Then put the date, and where we found him, by the Ekron bridge - give them something"}},
{"s2_c02_creek_rocks_007","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=25,400|mood=sad|world=water",{1,"Why does Caleb keep putting creek rocks on his sister's grave?",2,"Says he saw it in a library book once",1,"There's forty rocks on there now",2,"Then he's been out there forty times - leave him his rocks"}},
{"s2_c02_dog_digging_008","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,200|mood=grim|world=rain",{1,"Dog's been digging at the end of the row",2,"Which one?",1,"The Wilkins boy, we didn't go deep enough, it was raining and we were in a hurry",2,"Two more feet of dirt on him today, chain the dog up nights, it's not the dog's fault either"}},
{"s2_c02_hum_at_grave_009","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,400|hour=17,20|mood=sad",{1,"Should we sing something?",2,"Singing carries",3,"Hum it, then, we all know the tune",1,"I don't know the words past the first verse anyhow",2,"Nobody does, that's why they put the books in the pews"}},
{"s2_c02_birthday_pancakes_010","any",3,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|mood=warm",{1,"Sadie's eight today - pancakes, flour, water, the last of the sorghum",2,"Candle?",1,"Found a birthday candle in the junk drawer, half of one - it's blue",3,"Do we sing?",2,"Whisper-sing, all of us, real close around her so she can hear it"}},
{"s2_c02_road_map_wrapping_011","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|mood=warm",{1,"Wrapped his present in a road map, the Kentucky one",2,"What's under all that Kentucky?",1,"His daddy's pocketknife, the one with the bone handle",2,"He's thirteen, that's the right year for it",1,"I folded it so Muldraugh's on top, where he was born"}},
{"s2_c02_nobody_remembered_012","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|mood=warm|world=building",{1,"Not one of you said a word to me all day",2,"About what?",1,"I'm forty - today, forty years old",3,"We know - go look in the root cellar",1,"What's in the root cellar?",3,"Go look, and act surprised - Ronnie worked real hard on it"}},
{"s2_c02_his_corners_013","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|hour=16,5|mood=sad",{1,"Today would've been Dale's birthday - fifty-one",2,"You want to do anything?",1,"He always took the corners off the cornbread, said they had the most crust",2,"Then nobody takes a corner tonight"}},
{"s2_c02_truck_air_014","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=330,400|hour=12,18|mood=warm|world=vehicle,door,window,cold",{1,"Birthday present - get in the truck, roll the windows up",2,"It's a hundred degrees in that truck",1,"Not for long, I saved a gallon of gas for this, five minutes of air conditioning",3,"Can I get in too?",1,"It's her birthday, so you're allowed to hover by the door when she opens it",2,"Oh, oh, Lord, it's cold, nobody talk to me"}},
{"s2_c02_saltine_cake_015","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|mood=funny",{1,"It's a cake",2,"It's saltines stacked up with peanut butter in between",1,"Seven layers, candle in the middle - it's a cake",2,"Then happy birthday to me, it's a real good cake"}},
{"s2_c02_sixteen_field_016","any",2,"reg=family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|mood=funny|world=road",{1,"I remember turning sixteen and expecting somebody to hand me car keys",2,"Did you get to drive?",1,"In the bottom field, first gear, stopping whenever Dad hollered",2,"When did you get to take it on the road?",1,"After a lot more hollering. First lesson was putting the belt on, not finding the gas"}},
{"s2_c02_porch_post_017","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=15,400|hour=4,11|mood=warm|world=building",{1,"Twenty-two years today",2,"I know it - Carved it in the porch post this morning while you slept",1,"Last year you forgot",2,"Last year I had a calendar to forget with"}},
{"s2_c02_mutter_mantel_clock_018","any",1,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=15,400|hour=18,23|mood=sad",{1,"Sunday, wind the mantel clock, fourteen turns, not fifteen",1,"Fifteen and the spring binds, he told me that every Sunday for thirty years",1,"Fourteen - there, still running, Walt"}},
{"s2_c02_quilt_hoop_019","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=120,260|hour=17,22|mood=sad",{1,"Mamaw's quilt was still in the hoop, double wedding ring - three rings short of done",2,"You know how to quilt?",1,"No, I've picked out every stitch I've put in, twice",2,"Show me what you're doing, four hands can do it wrong twice as fast"}},
{"s2_c02_sourdough_crock_020","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,300|mood=sad",{1,"Carol's sourdough starter's still alive, in the crock on the top shelf",2,"How? It's been months",1,"I feed it, flour and water every other day - same as she did",2,"We're near about out of flour",1,"It eats before I do"}},
{"s2_c02_burn_day_021","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=15,200|mood=grim|world=building",{1,"Tomorrow's burn day, two out by the ditch, and the one off the Tackett porch",2,"Wind's out of the south - Smoke'll come right over the house",3,"So we let them lay another day and wait on a north wind?",1,"We wait, flies can have one more day - I'm not breathing in a Tackett"}},
{"s2_c02_beans_after_022","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=fresh,seasoned|day=20,45|hour=4,11|mood=sad",{1,"Buried a man this morning, then ate a whole plate of beans at noon",2,"You were hungry",1,"Three weeks ago I couldn't eat supper the day the neighbor's cat got run over",2,"Three weeks ago you were somebody else - eat your supper too"}},
{"s2_c02_dig_one_ahead_023","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=90,130|mood=grim",{1,"Dig one ahead, I say, before the ground freezes up",2,"Dig a grave for nobody?",3,"For somebody, we just don't know who yet",2,"That's the worst idea I ever heard, hand me the pick"}},
{"s2_c02_garden_report_024","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=30,400|hour=17,21|mood=sad",{1,"Who's Marlene talking to out by the graves?",2,"Bobby, tells him what's coming up in the garden - every evening",1,"Does it help?",2,"Bobby hated gardening, so I figure it helps her"}},
{"s2_c02_say_words_025","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=20,300|mood=grim",{1,"Somebody say words - anybody",2,"I don't know the words",3,"He fixed the pump, he never once left the gate open, he shared his tobacco when he had two cans or one",1,"That's words"}},
{"s2_c02_dwayne_spelling_026","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=40,300|mood=funny",{1,"You spelled his name wrong on the cross - Dwayne's got a W",2,"I wrote it how he said it",1,"He'd have corrected you, he corrected the preacher at his own daddy's funeral",2,"Hand me the paint, I'm not having that man correct me from under there"}},
{"s2_c02_expecting_027","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=60,200|mood=warm",{1,"Lacey's expecting, she told me at the clothesline",2,"Here? Now?",3,"Babies don't check the news first",1,"She figures April - Mrs. Olvey says she'll see her through",2,"Mrs. Olvey is seventy-eight",3,"Mrs. Olvey had six of her own on a farmhouse bed - start saving towels"}},
{"s2_c02_baby_name_028","any",4,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=250,330|mood=funny",{1,"We can't keep calling her the baby",2,"Hope",3,"Too much, that's too much for a baby to carry around",4,"Name her after a town - Rosewood",1,"We're not from Rosewood",4,"Nobody's from Rosewood anymore - name's free"}},
{"s2_c02_washer_ring_029","any",3,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=90,400|mood=warm",{1,"Ray and Tina want to get married - Saturday",2,"Who's gonna do it? There's no preacher and no courthouse",3,"Granny Pruitt's the oldest, she says she'll say it",1,"Ring?",2,"Brass washer off the pump handle - Ray's been sanding it smooth all week when he thinks nobody's looking"}},
{"s2_c02_granny_ceremony_030","any",2,"reg=civilian,family|tmp=seasoned|day=90,400|hour=18,23|mood=funny",{1,"Granny Pruitt forgot the words halfway through and just said well, you're married, go on",2,"Best wedding I ever been to",1,"Only one I ever been to where nobody got drunk and fell in the cake",2,"Nothing to drink and no cake to fall in, that ain't behaving"}},
}
